## Question 1
Why is the list in RideManager typed ArrayList<Ride> and not ArrayList<Jeepney>?
Your answer: Cuz Ride is like the big main category, If you make it ArrayList<Jeepney>, you can ONLY put jeepneys in the list.
 But if you use ArrayList<Ride>, you can put jeepneys and other types of rides like buses or tricycles in there too so its way more flexible.

## Question 2
In showStudentDiscounts(), why must you check instanceof before the cast?
Your answer: Because if you try to force cast a ride into something it actually isn't, the whole program will freak out and crash
Checking instanceof first is like asking "hey, are you actually this type of ride?" before you cast it so your code don't break.